WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.630
PROFESSOR 1: So we are here today
with Professor Allen Kachalia.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.310
Allen is a physician.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.620
He's also a lawyer and a professor
at Harvard Medical School.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.620
ALLEN KACHALIA: When I
first went into medicine,

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.040
most of us who go into medicine, we
go in it to make patients feel better.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.954
We realize that we don't necessarily
always do that because mistakes

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:23.120
happen right in front of us.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.078
This is something is very preventable,
something that's in our control.

00:00:26.078 --> 00:00:29.688
There's no reason for most of the
mistakes that happen to happen.

00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:32.479
And we need to do a better job of
it because patients also trust us

00:00:32.479 --> 00:00:33.480
when they come into the hospital.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.810
I think many of us think
that when we go to hospitals,

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:39.230
they are safe places where we go to
recover where we go to get better.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:43.150
They shouldn't be places
where we go and get hurt.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.550
I think that I have a job
that has a great mix of work.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.591
I went into medicine simply
because I knew that I

00:00:47.591 --> 00:00:49.250
would enjoy taking care of patients.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.850
I added a law degree to my
education because I wanted

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.782
to move into policy work later in life.

00:00:54.782 --> 00:00:56.990
I wouldn't say lawyers are
the problem in the system.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.450
I'd say the system is the problem.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.930
In the United States, for every dollar
that we spend on liability insurance,

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:04.115
only about $0.40 makes it to a patient.

00:01:04.115 --> 00:01:05.740
And I think we can do better than that.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.512
Lawyers can help the system improve
by helping patients navigate

00:01:08.512 --> 00:01:10.720
the system when patients
have been wrongfully injured

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.060
and they can't get
access to compensation.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:16.370
They can help hold the right
systems and providers accountable.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:19.690
They can also help patients negotiate
a quicker resolution or a quicker

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:21.580
settlement earlier
when it's more merited.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.830
So they can really help us
deliver that accountability

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.724
signal that we want delivered.

00:01:25.724 --> 00:01:28.640
Because patients on their own may
not know how to navigate the system.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.590
So lawyers can really
help with that piece.

